{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/the-crossroads-continent/1546429-inktober-postings-and-story-with-art-redux-7-the-finale","id":1546429,"title":"Inktober postings and story with art Redux #7 - the finale","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Crossroads Continent"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-26T17:22:57-08:00","id":1546429,"title":"Inktober postings and story with art Redux #7 - the finale","content":"Inktober Redux7: The finale.<br /> <br /> Our adventurers are hot on the trail of the band of Bugbears who they are reasonably sure have grabbed the mysterious parcel. Into the hot lowlands jungle they go! It's good to have a ranger when things need tracking, and Cap'n M'udd leads the group, stopping every so often to confirm the trail of the crafty Bugbears. The Bugbears are experienced enough to assume they might be tracked, and so try various means to throw our crew off their trail - but the sea elf ranger keeps finding it again!<br /> <br /> It's hot, sticky, buggy. It stinks, and the sounds of wildlife are constant. Along the edge of a small branch of one of the rivers, they encounter a hulking, shambling mound of rotting vegetation, much as they had earlier as they moved up the river. Left alone, these creatures wander their lonely way through the wetlands, even though Alabaster insists on trying to convert them to his Sky God - which only triggers the creatures' predator instincts!<br /> <br /> Further north, they come across a large lake of black water and their old friend Asmodeus, the mercenary dwarf warrior, lost in the lowlands. Together, they build a raft to maneuver across the lake between all the cypress trees, and are ambushed by a clutch of Bullywugs who had waited under the water until the party was in a narrow space between two trees. Fighting their way clear with the propulsive help of the swimming sea elves, they have to leave Asmodeus clinging to a clump of cypress as the Bullywugs pursue them - he had fallen off the raft, and was waving them away as the sea elves outdistanced the frog men.<br /> <br /> Out of the wetlands and further north, the group were scrambling up a ridge when the Bugbears attacked, with Hugh getting pin-cushioned and knocked down the ridge by several Bugbear javelins! With the assistance of a large swamp crab that Cap'n M'udd had befriended, the Bugbears were almost all defeated and several were captured - except for their leader, who escaped into more dense vegetation with the parcel, after throwing off his chainmail that Alabaster had used a Druidic heat metal spell on!<br /> <br /> The party encountered a hermit monk gnome, dedicated to healing, who was not only willing to let the party rest in his hovel, but he healed several of them including the Bugbears. He, Dr. Hammie, M.D., agreed to help them retrieve the parcel as he felt like it was the best way to get them out of his neck of the forest. (Hammie, MD, being played by another &quot;drop-in&quot; player for that game session.)<br /> <br /> This led to a final encounter with the Bugbear leader, where he fought several of his own troops angry at him for running off and leaving them earlier (and happy with the gold the party already paid them), and a group of odd and strong fish-men who sprang out of a recessed pond and several hidden openings in the surrounding mounds. These creatures were unknown to the party, and included some sort of shaman or priest, as well as a leader who also knew unarmed combat and who went toe to fin with Dr Hammie in an exchange of punches and kicks!<br /> <br /> Ultimately, the surviving fish men retrieved the parcel from the Bugbear leader, threw him a pouch of gems, and disappeared into the depths of the pond (the assumption being that it was an entry into much deeper waterways under the earth.) From the Bugbears they got the story that they mercenaries had been hired to retrieve the stolen object by the fish men, and that it was something of great importance to them. With that information, the group worked its way back to the trading post, after saying bye to Dr Hammie, MD, and presented what they found to the post council.<br /> <br /> Their ships repaired, mostly, and with a new debt incurred by Malcolm at the Hungry Hydra, the party thought they would continue north, until the Bug asked them to help explore a strange opening he had discovered during their journey, and revealed the curiously carved rocks he had gathered there. The carvings were very similar to those on the post's pillar, so the archeologists on the council were very interested in sponsoring an expedition...<br /> <br /> And that's where we'll end our saga - for now!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}